      <h1>Codex</h1>
      <p class="lede">A codex to civilisation. The ancient Arabic script — twenty-eight letters — in the correct version, following the Hebrew letter sounds and the organisation of the letters. Hebrew in Arabic script. When they find it, they will know and experience the truth.</p>

      <p>The twenty-two Hebrew letters are the spine. The twenty-eight Arabic letters follow them — each one matched to its Hebrew brother by sound, in the Hebrew order, with the Hebrew values. And the Arabic script kept something the Hebrew script merged: the soft sounds of the seven doubles. Six extra letters hold them — the original sounds, restored. That is the codex: the sounds put back where they belong, and the whole alphabet standing in one order.</p>

      <h2>The seven doubles, restored</h2>
      <p>Seven letters are doubles. Each one speaks twice — hard and soft. The hard sound is the letter as it stands; the soft sound is the letter loosened. The Arabic script kept a letter for every soft sound, so here the doubles stand whole: the hard sound in its own letter, the soft sound in its own. Each double is king over a planet in the world, a day in the year, and a gate in the soul — and each carries a foundation.</p>

