      <p class="note">One Arabic letter, Fa, holds two soft sounds — Vet and Fe. The lips' soft sound is one sound in Arabic. And Pe hard — the P — has no Arabic letter at all; the Arabic tongue kept only the soft Fe. The gap is shown honestly. Resh is counted among the doubles, but it keeps one sound.</p>

      <h2>The twenty-eight</h2>
      <p>The whole alphabet, in abjad order — the ancient order the two tongues share. The chips filter by group; they are a filter, not the order. Mothers stand where they fall in the order, doubles carry their planet and their day, simples carry their sign, their Hebrew month, and their English dates. The last six are the restored sounds, and they carry the planet and the day of the double they restore.</p>
